Example only: references below are placeholders, not permanent IDs. In the Auto example sys_emp_id is absent. Use an Idempotency-Key header. Custom keys resolve through the pinned configuration and reject unknown, retired or unauthorised fields.
{  "component_id": "<registered_component_id>",  "operation": "REGISTER",  "configuration_version": 1,  "payload": {    "employee_name": "Example Employee",    "empid_entry_mode": "AUTO",    "father_name": "Example Father",    "nationality_id": "<approved_nationality_value_id>",    "national_id_type_id": "<approved_id_type_value_id>",    "id_number": "<entered_identifier>",    "custom_fields": {      "dob": "1995-06-15"    }  }}
{  "request_id": "<server_request_id>",  "status": "PENDING_APPROVAL",  "validation_errors": []}
MANUAL adds sys_emp_id as a required nonblank string. AUTO rejects that property. Reject unknown envelope and core-payload properties. DTO shape validation runs before component business validation; both run again as needed during approved execution. A changed configuration causes review/revalidation rather than silently adopting new requirements.

